{"content":[{"c":["CUSH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Eldest of Ham’s four sons (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.6","r":"Gen.10.6","rawR":"Gen.10.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.6","value":"Gen.10.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.8","r":"1Chr.1.8","rawR":"1Chr.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.8","value":"1Chr.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:8"},"). Because the other three (Egypt, Put, and Canaan) are place-names, it is likely that Cush also is a place. It is usually identified with Ethiopia. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cush (Place)"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Ethiopia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Ethiopia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Ethiopia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ethiopia"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Benjamite and presumably David’s enemy, mentioned in the title of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.7.1-17","r":"Ps.7.1-17","rawR":"Ps.7.1-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.7.1-17","value":"Ps.7.1-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 7"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"CushPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.6","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.6","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.8"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.7.1-17","rawQueryValue":"Ps.7.1-17","s